    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Beware of SSC traps where words coming between the subject and verb (e.g., 'along with', 'accompanied by') trick you into altering the verb form; the verb always agrees strictly with the main subject.",
        "In 'One of the + Plural Noun' structures, use a singular verb, but if followed by a relative pronoun ('who', 'which', 'that'), use a plural verb.",
        "Units of distance, time, money, and measurement take a singular verb when treated as a single collective quantity."
      ],
      "id": "6be5epi"
    },
